    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThere are few places within easy reach of Dublin that offer such a rare balance of tranquillity, natural beauty and connectivity. Positioned on the shores of the magnificent Rogerstown Estuary, Mystic is an exceptional contemporary residence where coastal living, modern comfort and effortless convenience come together in perfect harmony.\n\nExtending to approximately 147 sq.m (1,582sq.ft), this beautifully designed four-bedroom detached home enjoys an enviable waterfront setting with uninterrupted panoramic views across the estuary. From sunrise to sunset, the ever-changing seascape provides a captivating backdrop to daily life, while the property's sunny orientation ensures natural light fills the home throughout the day.\n\nDesigned with modern family living in mind, Mystic offers a thoughtful blend of open-plan spaces and more intimate reception rooms, creating a home that is equally suited to entertaining, family gatherings and the evolving needs of contemporary lifestyles. Whether enjoying time together in the heart of the home or working remotely in complete comfort, every aspect of the design has been carefully considered to maximise both the spectacular views and the quality of everyday living.\n\nFloor-to-ceiling glazing and generously proportioned rooms draw the surrounding landscape into the home, creating a seamless connection between the interior and the natural beauty beyond. The private rear garden provides a peaceful retreat, while ample parking further enhances the practicality of this outstanding residence.\nA Lifestyle Defined by Coast and Countryside\nMystic occupies a truly special position along one of Dublin's most scenic coastal stretches. \n\nRogerstown Estuary is renowned for its natural beauty, protected wildlife habitats and miles of picturesque shoreline, offering residents a lifestyle that feels wonderfully removed from the pace of city life.\nMorning walks along the estuary, sailing excursions from the nearby sailing club, rounds of golf at excellent local courses and afternoons spent exploring the beaches and coastal villages of North County Dublin all become part of everyday life. The surrounding landscape offers a sense of calm and connection to nature that is increasingly difficult to find, yet remains remarkably accessible.\n\nKnown as the 'Market Garden' of North Dublin, the vibrant seaside town of Rush is just moments away, providing an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, shops, schools and sporting facilities. The area has long been appreciated by those seeking a more relaxed pace of life without compromising on convenience.\nInternational Connectivity, Local Community\nFor international purchasers, returning expatriates and those seeking a distinguished Irish coastal residence, Mystic presents an exceptionally compelling proposition. Dublin Airport's Terminal 2 is approximately fifteen minutes away, placing global travel within effortless reach. The M1 motorway network and excellent transport links also ensure Dublin City Centre is easily accessible for business, cultural pursuits or commuting when required.\n\nThis unique combination of waterfront serenity, strong community spirit and world-class connectivity is increasingly sought after by buyers relocating to Ireland or returning home from overseas. Mystic offers the opportunity to establish roots within a welcoming semi-rural community while enjoying all the advantages of modern infrastructure and international accessibility.\n\nMystic is far more than a family home; it is a lifestyle destination. A place where estuary views replace urban skylines, where sailing and coastal walks begin at your doorstep, and where the demands of modern life are balanced by space, privacy and natural beauty.\nOffering contemporary luxury in one of North County Dublin's most picturesque coastal settings, Mystic represents a rare opportunity to acquire a remarkable home on Ireland's celebrated east coast."
      },
